WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.413 --> 00:00:04.570
-My first guests
are global pop music icons.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.273
They've had
four number-one songs

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:11.377
on the Billboard Hot 100
in less than a year.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:13.913
Their latest song,
"Permission to Dance,"

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:18.751
is out now, and it's available
on the "Butter" CD single.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:24.390
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome BTS!

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.325
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:33.099
♪♪

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.701
Come on!

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.770
Look at you guys!
Look at you!

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.372
Welcome back!

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:42.241
-What's popping? How you doing?

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.176
-Jimmy!

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.010
-Now, I'm doing great, guys.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.412
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:47.814
Yeah, I love those suspenders,
bud.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:51.017
Now, since
your first appearance,

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.820
we talked
about Grammy nominations

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.489
and what it would mean to you
every single time.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.623
Well, it finally happened.

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.291
"Dynamite" was nominated
for a Grammy.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:00.593
Congratulations on that.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.995
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.597
-Yeah, a Grammy!

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.700
-What was that like for you,
and how did it feel?

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.370
-Sorry for the cliche, but,
you know, it's really an honor.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.806
You know, it's one of the
biggest honors as an artist

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.876
for, of course,
throughout the world.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.378
And it's the first time
as a Korean,

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:22.482
and, you know, that's
so meaningful, so historic.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.351
And just,
we couldn't, like, realize it.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.587
And I'm so happy, so crazy,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.622
and so thankful for all the fans
all over the world.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.790
That's it.
-I have a good feeling

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.525
that you're gonna win a Grammy
soon enough,

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.827
because "Butter"
is number-one on the Hot 100

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.629
for the 7th week in a row.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.665
[ Cheers and applause ]
The video...

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.866
-Amazing!

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:46.606
-The video has almost
half a billion views.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.241
I have a feeling it's gonna be
the song of the summer.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:52.712
How did you know that "Butter"
was gonna work?

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.214
-Oh!
-[ Speaking in Korean ]

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.591
-Ah, yep.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:10.095
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:13.366
-I like in the "Butter" video,
at one point you spell out

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.301
army using your bodies.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.138
And I'm sure the army
appreciates it, too.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.807
Yeah. "A" I can get. Yeah.

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:26.045
"R" is pretty -- "R"
is pretty easy. It's like "R."

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.381
And them "M" would be this.

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:31.451
And then that, you know?

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.485
Anyways, you did it much cooler,
but I will say

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:38.157
Jin and Jungkook, tell me
about creating the "A,"

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.059
because that doesn't look
easy for me.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.261
-[ Laughs ]
-Ooh!

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:44.563
-[ Speaking in Korean ]
-[ Speaking in Korean ]

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:46.899
-Okay. Let's go. Let's go.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.235
-That's what I'm talking about!
-Let's go, let's go.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:52.905
-Yeah! Aw!
-Easy.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:57.576
-Easy peasy lemon squeezy!
-Easy peasy lemon squeezy.

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.479
-Yeah.
-Easy. Easy.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:02.015
-Easy peasy. It wasn't hard.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.382
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.351
You get it in one take, yeah.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:10.089
On Friday, you released the new
single "Permission to Dance."

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.391
Tell me how this song came
together.

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:16.862
-So, "PTD" is a song that will
get everybody's heart pumping

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:20.199
and dancing again, and, you
know, this is a, actually, gift

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:23.069
of Ed Sheeran, of course,
one of our friends.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.871
Mad respect. Big love to Ed.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.039
And we also prepared something
called

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.175
"Permission to Dance" Challenge
with YouTube Shorts,

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.477
so please stay tuned for more.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.878
"PTD," let's go.
-Wow.

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:35.648
Did you -- Do you remember
when you first met Ed Sheeran?

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:39.585
-Oh, we can't believe that we
haven't met him yet.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:42.020
And, you know, this is
the second project with him,

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.823
but we never met him yet.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:46.692
-Is that right? That's wild.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.695
I mean, 'cause I have some
ideas, and we actually have met.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:52.198
So, I know you better
than Ed Sheeran.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.399
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.134
-Oh, of course. Of course.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.237
-Yeah, so I have some song ideas
if you want.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:01.274
You know, if you want to work
in the "Butter" category,

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.809
I can go all through
the dairy aisle.

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:08.080
Whatever you think of, you let
me know and we'll get together.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.016
Just get on the phone,
we'll Zoom, we'll FaceTime.

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:12.751
We'll figure it out.
-Let's go!

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:15.588
-Zoom, Zoom, Zoom! Let's go.
-Maybe cheesecake or cereal.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:18.290
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.226
-Yeah, that's what I'll do. I'll
work on "Cereal" with you guys.

00:04:21.226 --> 00:04:25.798
I was excited to see you guys go
on tour, "Map of the Soul" tour,

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.699
and then the pandemic happened.

00:04:27.699 --> 00:04:29.201
I didn't get a chance to see it

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:31.337
or open for you guys.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.105
And so -- You never asked.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:37.309
But I was thinking when --
when will you go back on tour,

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:40.780
and what will that feel like
when you do go back on tour?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.948
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:45.551
-Yeah! Make some noise! Yeah!

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.986
-Whoo-hoo!

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.022
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:54.260
-This is what we want, and
this is what we're gonna feel

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.528
when we're back on tour.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.630
We want to do the
"make some noise" thing again.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.133
-Getting out there, even for
like 10 people, then 50,

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:05.605
and now finally a full audience,
it's emotional just for me.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:10.176
I'm just preparing you
for an emotional...

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.144
an emotional first performance,
yeah.

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:15.014
Wear sunglasses.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.417
-Get ready, guys, get ready.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.718
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you!

00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:22.822
-Speaking of sunglasses,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:26.959
I have a photo of your first
show eight years ago

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:29.328
when BTS just started.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.729
Can you look at yourselves here?

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:33.065
Which one of you guys
is wearing the sunglasses

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:36.034
in the darkest room
I've ever seen in my life?

00:05:36.034 --> 00:05:37.236
-Oh!
-Oh!

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.673
-Wow.
-Actually, it's me...

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.374
-Oh!

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:45.511
-It's very hilarious.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.113
-Ooh.
-Jimin! Jimin, turn around!

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:50.215
-Jimin!
-Jimin, turn around.

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:52.919
Jimin, look --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:55.988
-Be confident. Be confident.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.490
-Oh, my goodness.
It's great.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:00.292
But what goes through your mind
when you see something --

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.195
I won't show it anymore.

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:04.196
But what do you think when you
see that?

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:06.365
That was only eight years ago,
not too long ago.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:11.670
[ All speaking in Korean ]

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.138
-Yeah.
-We got --

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:15.541
Actually, we think we got
handsome.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.809
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.644
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.780
-Oh, no, hey. No.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.347
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.347 --> 00:06:23.916
I think...

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.318
I think you've always had that.
I think you've always had that.

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:29.355
Now, look, I want to
get to the bottom

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.490
of some BTS rumors
that are out there.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.894
More with BTS when we come back,
everybody. Come on back!

